Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• `stations.usaf`: primary station identifier – will be matched to `gsod2019.stn`.  
• `stations.wban`: secondary station identifier – joined to `gsod2019.wban` to make sure we are matching the correct station when the USAF id is not unique by itself.  
• `stations.begin`: first date (yyyymmdd) in the station’s period‐of‑record – used to keep only stations that began on or before 20000101.  
• `stations.end`: last date (yyyymmdd) in the station’s period‐of‑record – used to make sure the station was still operating on or after 20190630.  
• `gsod2019.stn`: the USAF station id in the daily observations – primary key for joining to `stations.usaf`.  
• `gsod2019.wban`: WBAN id – secondary key for joining to `stations.wban`.  
• `gsod2019.temp`, `gsod2019.max`, `gsod2019.min`: daily mean / maximum / minimum temperatures – must all be different from the missing sentinel 9999.9 to be considered “valid”.  
• `gsod2019.year`, `gsod2019.mo`, `gsod2019.da`: date parts – together guarantee we are looking at 2019 only (all rows in `gsod2019` are from 2019 anyway).  

Typical conditions we will use  

1. Non‑missing temperature fields:  
   temp   <> 9999.9 AND  
   max    <> 9999.9 AND  
   min    <> 9999.9  

2. Period of record restriction:  
   CAST(begin AS INT64) <= 20000101 AND  
   CAST(end   AS INT64) >= 20190630  

3. 90 % of possible days:  
   valid_day_cnt >= 0.9 * 365   (i.e., ≥ 329 days in 2019)  

Ten exploratory / step‑by‑step BigQuery SQL snippets
----------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1. Quick look at the daily data for 2019
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2019`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Check how many total daily rows exist in the 2019 file
SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_2019_rows
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2019`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Verify the occurrences of the missing sentinel in temp/max/min
SELECT
  SUM(CASE WHEN temp = 9999.9 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)      AS missing_temp,
  SUM(CASE WHEN max  = 9999.9 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)      AS missing_max,
  SUM(CASE WHEN min  = 9999.9 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)      AS missing_min
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2019`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Sample rows where all three temperature fields are valid
SELECT stn, wban, year, mo, da, temp, max, min
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2019`
WHERE temp <> 9999.9
  AND max  <> 9999.9
  AND min  <> 9999.9
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Count valid‑temperature days per station in 2019
SELECT
  stn,
  wban,
  COUNT(1) AS valid_days_2019
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2019`
WHERE temp <> 9999.9
  AND max  <> 9999.9
  AND min  <> 9999.9
GROUP BY stn, wban
ORDER BY valid_days_2019 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. List stations whose period of record began ≤ 2000‑01‑01
--    and continued past 2019‑06‑30
SELECT usaf, wban, begin, end
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations`
WHERE CAST(begin AS INT64) <= 20000101
  AND CAST(end   AS INT64) >= 20190630
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Join daily data with the filtered station list
--    (retains only rows from stations meeting the period criteria)
SELECT
  g.stn,
  g.wban,
  g.temp, g.max, g.min
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2019` AS g
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations` AS s
  ON g.stn  = s.usaf
 AND g.wban = s.wban
WHERE CAST(s.begin AS INT64) <= 20000101
  AND CAST(s.end   AS INT64) >= 20190630
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Compute valid‑temperature day counts for those stations
--    that satisfy period‑of‑record requirements
WITH station_filter AS (
  SELECT usaf, wban
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations`
  WHERE CAST(begin AS INT64) <= 20000101
    AND CAST(end   AS INT64) >= 20190630
)
SELECT
  g.stn,
  g.wban,
  COUNT(1) AS valid_days_2019
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2019` AS g
JOIN station_filter AS f
  ON g.stn  = f.usaf
 AND g.wban = f.wban
WHERE g.temp <> 9999.9
  AND g.max  <> 9999.9
  AND g.min  <> 9999.9
GROUP BY g.stn, g.wban
ORDER BY valid_days_2019 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Apply the 90 % (≥ 329 days) threshold
WITH station_filter AS (
  SELECT usaf, wban
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations`
  WHERE CAST(begin AS INT64) <= 20000101
    AND CAST(end   AS INT64) >= 20190630
),
valid_day_counts AS (
  SELECT
    g.stn,
    g.wban,
    COUNT(1) AS valid_days_2019
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2019` AS g
  JOIN station_filter AS f
    ON g.stn  = f.usaf
   AND g.wban = f.wban
  WHERE g.temp <> 9999.9
    AND g.max  <> 9999.9
    AND g.min  <> 9999.9
  GROUP BY g.stn, g.wban
)
SELECT *
FROM valid_day_counts
WHERE valid_days_2019 >= 0.9 * 365   -- ≥ 329
ORDER BY valid_days_2019 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final query: number of stations that met every requirement
WITH station_filter AS (
  SELECT usaf, wban
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations`
  WHERE CAST(begin AS INT64) <= 20000101
    AND CAST(end   AS INT64) >= 20190630
),
valid_day_counts AS (
  SELECT
    g.stn,
    g.wban,
    COUNT(1) AS valid_days_2019
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2019` AS g
  JOIN station_filter AS f
    ON g.stn  = f.usaf
   AND g.wban = f.wban
  WHERE g.temp <> 9999.9
    AND g.max  <> 9999.9
    AND g.min  <> 9999.9
  GROUP BY g.stn, g.wban
)
SELECT COUNT(*) AS stations_reaching_90pct_of_full_year
FROM valid_day_counts
WHERE valid_days_2019 >= 0.9 * 365;   -- 329 days or more
LIMIT 20;
```

Run the last query to obtain the required count of NOAA GSOD stations that (a) began on or before 1 Jan 2000, (b) were active at least through 30 Jun 2019, (c) recorded valid temp/max/min values on at least 329 days of 2019 – i.e., 90 % or more of the 365 possible days.
